{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15322709","formula":"C₃₃H₃₈O₆","hill":"C33H38O6","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":33.0,"H":38.0,"O":6.0},"names":{"en":"Glycerol phenylbutyrate"},"descriptions":{"en":"Glycerol phenylbutyrate (INNTooltip International Nonproprietary Name, USANTooltip United States Adopted Name), sold under the brand name Ravicti, is a nitrogen-binding agent medication used for chronic management of certain urea cycle disorders. The medication reduces the harmful buildup of ammonia in the body. It functions as a prodrug of phenylbutyric acid, which conjugates with glutamine to form phenylacetylglutamine, facilitating ammonia excretion via the kidneys It was developed by Hyperion Therapeutics based on the existing medication sodium phenylbutyrate, and received FDA approval in February 2013."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":10482134,"mass":530.6,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=C(C=C1)CCCC(=O)OCC(COC(=O)CCCC2=CC=CC=C2)OC(=O)CCCC3=CC=CC=C3","inchikey":"ZSDBFLMJVAGKOU-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2,3-bis(4-phenylbutanoyloxy)propyl 4-phenylbutanoate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"10482134","atoms":77,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-9.461,"y":-3.058,"z":0.359,"el":"C"},{"x":-8.975,"y":-3.827,"z":-0.697,"el":"C"},{"x":-7.607,"y":-4.084,"z":-0.804,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.713,"y":-3.577,"z":0.149,"el":"C"},{"x":-7.211,"y":-2.8,"z":1.204,"el":"C"},{"x":-8.579,"y":-2.544,"z":1.309,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.233,"y":-3.838,"z":0.024,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.539,"y":-2.752,"z":-0.799,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.045,"y":-3.024,"z":-0.919,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.377,"y":-1.968,"z":-1.759,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.042,"y":-2.125,"z":-2.925,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.195,"y":-0.83,"z":-1.038,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.617,"y":0.286,"z":-1.735,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.126,"y":0.446,"z":-1.414,"el":"C"},{"x":0